	<digest>
		Korg OTA dual-amplifier modified Sallen-Key topology nonlinear filter emulation with simultaneous outputs
	</digest>
	<description>
		<b>evi.korgms20~</b> is a 'max define' for the <o>evi_korgms20</o>.gendsp gen~ abstraction.
		Because evi.korgms20~ is a 'max define' it also accepts all messages and attributes that a <o>gen~</o> object does. <br />
		<br />
		The 'KLM' OTA chip was found in the later MS-20s and other Korg synthesisers - it is different to the earlier 'Korg 35' single-amplifier unbuffered Korg chip found in the earlier MS-20s and MS-10 and also in the 'monotron' series. This Korg filter sits inbetween the more broken <o>evi.korgms10~</o> and the more stable <o>evi.korgms20.select~</o>. It is aggressive but predictable. <br />
	</description>
